{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>מזי רעב.</b> The burning of hunger, from (Daniel 2) למזא לאתונא. For from the side of hunger, the natural heat within them burns them, since they are healthy and have nothing to eat, and they are consumed by the disease of consumption (שחפת)." "<b>וקטב מרירי.</b> It is the cutting off of the bitterness of the air, in the language of (Job 3:5) יבעתוהו כמרירי יום, and this is (Psalms 91:6) ומקטב ישוד צהרים, and this is pestilence (הדבר). And he mentioned here four decrees: famine, pestilence, wild beast, and sword."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:53:18.868242012Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}